              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda Sargent Meade"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This pie is the BEST!! So easy too! Just a few notes: \n\n3/4 cup Key Lime juice is = to about 20 Key limes. I used a garlic press to squeeze the limes quickly and easily (cut limes in half). \n\n3 Cups of sweetened condensed milk = about 2 cans. \n\nPerfect recipe! Impress your friends and enjoy!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MOONMYST17"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe. I am from Florida and have had many key lime pies when visiting key west. This is the most authentic tasting pie I have ever made at home. What is best is that it is SO SIMPLE! You can literally whip it up in no time. I used home made whipped topping (heavy whipping cream with a touch of sugar and vanilla) and spread it over the entire pie. I made this for my husbands birthday dinner party. I have since made this pie 3 more times. Everytime we are invited to dinner friends ask me to make this pie for them, it is PERFECT! Do not try another key lime pie recipe on this site, this is the only one you need!",
            "datePublished": "2008-07-04T10:13:46.717Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Phyllis"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My second review after making (and sharing) about three pies. Awesome, awesome recipe, and couldn't be easier!! I found that two 14-oz. cans of condensed milk was perfect - I can't imagine using three. I also didn't bother with the zest and didn't feel the lack. Nice, creamy and tart pie. So good it makes ya want to slap your mamma!",
            "datePublished": "2007-09-11T13:33:21.600Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "iluv2cook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Incredibly delicious pie and SO easy to put together! I’ve made a few time following the instructions. I’ve also baked just the filling with no crust and it’s a no mistake pie. Delicious every time. This time around, I made 1/2 recipe and baked in the airfryer with some adjustments. I used 1 can of 14oz condensed milk, 1/2 cup of lime juice (100% juice store bought) 1/4 cup of sour cream and zest of 1/2 a big orange (didn’t have fresh lime) and a sprinkle of shredded coconut on top and that was exactly enough to fill 6 small pre made graham cracker crusts (Keebler). So I preheated the airfryer for 5 mins on 400. Dropped the temp to 350 and put the little pie shells in there to pre bake for about 5 mins. Took them out, scooped the filling in the shells sprinkled the tops with some coconut flakes and baked for 4 mins. After cooled, put in the fridge. Turned out amazing! And such a good dessert to make in a pinch. Super recommend.",
            "datePublished": "2023-01-08T15:13:23.739Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BraveDonut6903"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I use 2 cans of condensed milk, increase the lime juice a bit, and bake for 13-15 minutes. The best!",
