              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FunkyBao6734"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe was great! My husband had been craving Key Lime Pie flavor anything so I made this for his birthday yesterday. I had never made any key lime dessert before and this was great! I preferred this recipe because I didn’t want to use eggs and the sour cream was a great substitute! I only used 2 cans of condensed milk, extra lime zest, and basic lime juice. I let it bake in the oven at 350 for 10 minutes (no bubbles appeared on top but it was very firm). Next time I think I’ll freeze the pie a bit before serving because it is so creamy and add more lime juice or zest for a more tart flavor. Our family really enjoyed it and my husband was satisfied!",
